  "notes": "Luba-Kasai (Tshiluba/Ciluba), Guthrie L.31, Bantu language of Kasai region, DR Congo; one of the country's four national languages. Five-vowel system a/e/i/o/u with a length distinction. Standard orthography uses the digraphs ng, ny and sh but no q, r, x. Prenasalized stops (mb, nd, ng, nk, mp, nt) and the affricate tsh /tʃ/ (with its prenasalized counterpart ntsh) are single phonemes. Dialects differ in tone; the standard orthography does not mark tone.",
